---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Disclaimer from "../../../components/Disclaimer.astro";

const template = `To the Public Information Officer of [AGENCY/CITY NAME]:

Under the Texas Public Information Act, Texas Government Code Chapter 552, I am requesting copies of the following public records:

1. The current contract(s), including any amendments, between [AGENCY/CITY NAME] and Flock Safety, Inc. (or any automated license plate reader / ALPR vendor).
2. Any policy or procedure governing who may query the ALPR/Flock camera system, for what purposes, and under what authorization.
3. Audit logs or search-history reports of ALPR/Flock system queries for the period [START DATE] through [END DATE], including which agency or officer made each search and the stated reason, to the extent such logs are not confidential under law.
4. Any records of data-sharing agreements with agencies outside [CITY/COUNTY], including any out-of-state agencies.

If any portion of this request is denied or withheld, please cite the specific statutory exception you are relying on, as required by Chapter 552.

Under Section 552.221, a governmental body must, within 10 business days of receiving this request, either provide the requested information or certify in writing when it will be available. Please treat this as a request for information "promptly" available, per that section.

If there are any fees associated with fulfilling this request, please notify me before incurring costs above [DOLLAR AMOUNT, OPTIONAL].

Please send responsive records to:
[YOUR NAME]
[YOUR EMAIL OR MAILING ADDRESS]

Thank you,
[YOUR NAME]
[DATE]`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Texas Public Information Act Request Template" description="Template for requesting Flock Safety contracts and ALPR audit logs under the Texas Public Information Act.">
  <article class="template-page">
    <p><a href="/act/">← Back to Act in Your City</a></p>
    <h1>Texas Public Information Act Request</h1>

    <Disclaimer text="This template is provided for general public education and is not legal advice. Confirm current requirements and any fee rules with the agency or an attorney before submitting." />

    <p>
      Under Texas Government Code Chapter 552 (the Public Information Act), a
      governmental body must respond within 10 business days of receiving a
      request — either producing the records or certifying in writing when
      they'll be available (Tex. Gov't Code § 552.221). Audit logs are one of
      the most useful documents you can request: they're often how ALPR
      misuse gets discovered in the first place.
    </p>

    <pre id="pia-template">{template}</pre>
    <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy-target="pia-template">Copy to clipboard</button>

    <p>
      Once you get a response, consider <a href="/database/submit">submitting</a>{" "}
      anything notable you find to our abuse database.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .template-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  pre {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    background: rgba(232, 232, 232, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 232, 232, 0.15);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .copy-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-fg, #e8e8e8);
    color: var(--color-fg, #e8e8e8);
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".copy-btn").forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const targetId = btn.dataset.copyTarget;
      const el = targetId && document.getElementById(targetId);
      if (!el) return;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(el.textContent ?? "");
        const original = btn.textContent;
        btn.textContent = "Copied!";
        setTimeout(() => {
          btn.textContent = original;
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        // clipboard API unavailable/denied - user can still select+copy manually
      }
    });
  });
</script>
